00:00:00.510 --> 00:00:37.269
Okay.

00:00:37.269 --> 00:00:42.879
You might remember that Donald Trump, uh,
once had this letter that Kim Jong Un sent

00:00:42.879 --> 00:00:46.780
him, I think he might've called it a beautiful
letter or something like that.

00:00:46.780 --> 00:00:52.559
Donald Trump had reporters in the room at
that time and he may have asked to go off

00:00:52.559 --> 00:00:55.699
the record in terms of the contents or maybe
not.

00:00:55.699 --> 00:00:57.629
And he held up the letter.

00:00:57.629 --> 00:01:03.289
And from what we have learned so far, a reporter
from Time magazine held up his camera to take

00:01:03.289 --> 00:01:08.440
a picture and Donald Trump said, and it's
sort of confusing and muddled and erratic,

00:01:08.440 --> 00:01:10.760
like a lot of what Donald Trump says.

00:01:10.760 --> 00:01:16.240
But what Trump said according to the transcript
is, uh, excuse me, under section two.

00:01:16.240 --> 00:01:21.010
Well, you can go to prison instead because
if you use, if you use the photograph you

00:01:21.010 --> 00:01:25.360
took of the letter that I gave you and time
tries to continue talking about the topic

00:01:25.360 --> 00:01:30.820
of the interview, do you believe that people
should be and Trump interims interrupts confidentially.

00:01:30.820 --> 00:01:34.860
I didn't give it to you to take photographs
of it, so don't play that game with me.

00:01:34.860 --> 00:01:35.920
Let me just tell you something.

00:01:35.920 --> 00:01:37.100
You take a look.

00:01:37.100 --> 00:01:41.370
Time says, I'm sorry Mr President, were you
threatening me with prison time?

00:01:41.370 --> 00:01:45.530
And Trump says, well, I told you the following,
I told you you can look at this off the record.

00:01:45.530 --> 00:01:48.690
That doesn't mean you take out your camera
and start taking pictures of it.

00:01:48.690 --> 00:01:49.690
Okay?

00:01:49.690 --> 00:01:50.690
So I hope you don't have a picture of it.

00:01:50.690 --> 00:01:54.230
I know you were very quick to pull it out
even you were surprised to see that you can't

00:01:54.230 --> 00:01:55.320
do that stuff.

00:01:55.320 --> 00:01:58.920
So go have fun with your story because I'm
sure it will be the 28th horrible story I

00:01:58.920 --> 00:02:03.860
have in Time magazine because I never, I mean,
it's incredible.

00:02:03.860 --> 00:02:08.160
With all I've done and the success I've had,
the way that Time magazine writes is absolutely

00:02:08.160 --> 00:02:09.439
incredible.

00:02:09.439 --> 00:02:15.829
Fascinatingly, this riled him up so much that
he then went into a huge rant about no collusion,

00:02:15.829 --> 00:02:19.599
no obstruction as a result of a photographer
taking a picture.

00:02:19.599 --> 00:02:24.050
It is just so incredible to read a transcript
of Donald Trump's scolding or report or for

00:02:24.050 --> 00:02:29.180
taking a picture of something that Trump gave
confidentially, which he doesn't even understand

00:02:29.180 --> 00:02:34.799
the meaning of while he has given up secrets
from allies to Russians in the Oval Office.

00:02:34.799 --> 00:02:40.659
I mean, it's a jarring juxtaposition of what
Trump says and what Trump does.

00:02:40.659 --> 00:02:45.500
And it's really important to understand here
when Trump says he gave something confidentially.

00:02:45.500 --> 00:02:47.599
Confidential is a classification of documents.

00:02:47.599 --> 00:02:53.510
You can't just yell out this is confidential
or you know, this pen is top secret and make

00:02:53.510 --> 00:02:58.760
it so, and it's also really important to understand
that it's Trump who shouldn't be showing things

00:02:58.760 --> 00:03:01.269
to people who don't have the correct clearances.

00:03:01.269 --> 00:03:06.650
And more importantly, Trump and his aides
remember, have bragged endlessly about how

00:03:06.650 --> 00:03:11.859
Trump can declassify anything he wants by
showing it to whoever he wants.

00:03:11.859 --> 00:03:17.749
If Trump shows someone the picture, then he
has decided that it's okay for them to see

00:03:17.749 --> 00:03:18.749
it.

00:03:18.749 --> 00:03:23.849
It's also really funny that Trump mentioned
section two and then he seemed to realize

00:03:23.849 --> 00:03:25.519
he didn't know what he was talking about.

00:03:25.519 --> 00:03:28.079
Let's put the transcript back up on the screen
for a moment.

00:03:28.079 --> 00:03:31.910
Trump started to say, excuse me, under section
two.

00:03:31.910 --> 00:03:35.310
And then he kind of went away from that and
said, well, you can go to prison instead.

00:03:35.310 --> 00:03:42.669
I guess he means article two of the constitution
or maybe section two of article two during

00:03:42.669 --> 00:03:44.019
the same confused interview.

00:03:44.019 --> 00:03:49.200
He seemed to be using the term section two
an article to uh, kind of interchangeably.

00:03:49.200 --> 00:03:52.219
Like maybe they're the same thing and he doesn't
know what he's talking about.

00:03:52.219 --> 00:03:55.959
Article two has two sections of the constitution.

00:03:55.959 --> 00:04:00.209
Section one establishes basically how the
president and vice president are to be elected

00:04:00.209 --> 00:04:02.469
and served four year terms.

00:04:02.469 --> 00:04:07.239
Section two of article two talks about the
president being the head of the executive

00:04:07.239 --> 00:04:12.199
branch of government and the commander in
chief of the armed forces who on earth knows

00:04:12.199 --> 00:04:17.650
what Donald Trump was talking about when he
mentioned section two and then article too,

00:04:17.650 --> 00:04:21.030
but at least at some point he seemed to have
the presence of mind to realize he doesn't

00:04:21.030 --> 00:04:23.220
actually know what the hell he's talking about.

00:04:23.220 --> 00:04:24.500
This is Trump though.

00:04:24.500 --> 00:04:25.500
Okay.

00:04:25.500 --> 00:04:29.300
When he was in private business, he would
threaten to sue anyone in business that he

00:04:29.300 --> 00:04:30.300
didn't like.

00:04:30.300 --> 00:04:34.420
That was his strategy and based on what we
know from Michael Cohen is former personal

00:04:34.420 --> 00:04:36.760
attorney, that was a pretty effective strategy.

00:04:36.760 --> 00:04:41.990
Sicking Michael Cohen, the attack dog on people
